  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADF14 Promissory Notes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is the UK&#x2019;s 13th replenishment to the concessional arm of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to fund concessional support to its poorest member countries to 2028. The ADB provides loans to wealthier developing members, and concessional loans or grants to its poorer members via the fund. The Business Case notes ADF 14 envisages a substantial uplift from $4 billion to $5 billion (though roughly constant &#x2013; 1% up - in real terms), with the ADB itself funding half the increase and nearly half (47%) of the overall total, &#x201c;a historic high&#x201d;1. It states that key foci of this replenishment round are to increase the level of transfer from ABD&#x2019;s net income, a stronger ($1.3 bn) offer for the Pacific small island developing states (SIDS), a new &#x2018;community window&#x2019; of $1.15bn in offers for Afghanistan ($815m), Myanmar ($200m), and Rohingya refugees ($100m)2 and increased focus on climate and gender impacts ($437m for adaptation and $194m for gender).</narrative>
  </description>
